# ---------- Flutter / Dart ----------
# `bin/` above is a .NET build-output rule, but it matches a directory of that name at *any*
# depth — which silently swallowed every Dart package's CLI entry point. `dart run <pkg>` looks
# for `bin/<pkg>.dart`, so an ignored bin/ means the tool works for whoever wrote it and is
# missing for everyone who clones the repo. `praxy_codegen`'s entry point was in exactly that
# state, uncommitted since the package was created, despite being the documented codegen command.
# The directory itself has to be re-included, not just its contents: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation on the files inside would never be consulted.
# Each entry is a directory of *source* that happens to be named bin/. They are listed
# individually rather than as `sdk/**/bin/` because sdk/dotnet/*/bin/ genuinely is .NET build
# output and must stay ignored — a blanket negation here would start committing DLLs.
!sdk/flutter/*/bin/
!sdk/flutter/*/bin/**
!sdk/generator/bin/
!sdk/generator/bin/**
.dart_tool/
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/
build/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
*.iml
.idea/

